--- body ---
Author ratifies a disposable cache and clarifies that global ETA means a
completion clock time. Rulings are recorded in DECISIONS.md and SPEC.md R22.
Cache native inspection hints and latest successful timing per attachment;
do not persist active tasks or failures. Source hash/processor changes and
pack fingerprint changes invalidate reuse. No text, title or source path is
stored. Corrupt or missing cache falls back to inspection.

Storage: `sdt-sitter-cache.jsonl` in Zotero's data directory. Compact at the
first completed census per activation, then append changed derived records
only; unchanged sweeps do not rewrite the cache. This is not an authoritative
work queue. Serialize writes across addon reactivations. A write failure must
not fail native extraction. Quantile fitting is memoized per fitted sample
array, avoiding a sort for every pending item on every UI refresh.

Show estimated local completion date/time and low/high scenarios. If the
active document exceeds the empirical upper duration, say the estimate is
exceeded instead of reporting completion now. Code-level panel feedback:
`verification/SDT-SITTER-UI-PANEL.md`.

Passing native integration, including cache reuse and observation restoration:
`bench/results/sdt-sitter-launch-2026-09-05/cache-and-progress.json`.
Unit cases in `tests/sdt_sitter_scheduler.mjs` cover source/version/fingerprint
invalidation, corrupt input, pruning and unchanged-cache dirty tracking.
